   "claims": [
    "To enter a number in scientific notation use a carat ^ to indicate the powers of 10.",
    "b is the power of 10 required so that the scientific notation is mathematically equivalent to the original number.",
    "Write your scientific notation number as a x 10^b and read it as \"a times 10 to the power of b.\" Remove trailing 0's only if they were originally to the left of the decimal point.",
    "E notation is basically the same as scientific notation except that the letter e is substituted for \"x 10^\"."
   ],
